Package: kelixip-mod-mcu-presence
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.ives.fr/
Depends: kelixip (= @VERSION@), kelixip-mod-mcu (= @VERSION@), kelixip-mod-presence (= @VERSION@)
Description: Conference rooms as presentities, for kelixip
 The link between the conference mixer and the presence collection: each
 conference room is a presentity, sip:<did>@<domain>, open while it runs, open
 and busy when it is full, closed while its media server is lost. A watcher
 subscribes to a room alone or in its buddy list, as it would to a user. Enable
 it with a [module.mcu_presence] block in config.toml, next to [module.mcu] and
 [module.presence].
 .
 The payload is BEAM bytecode, but the package is architecture-dependent on
 purpose: it must be built and shipped alongside the core whose embedded ERTS
 will load it.
